<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78746" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράσῑτ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who eats at the table of
				another, and repays him with flattery and buffoonery,
			parasite</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arar.
				16
			</span></i>, etc.; name of plays by <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ Παρασίτου</span>, title of
			work by <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενῆς π. τραπέζης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.346
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Autom.
			</span></i>) : metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθὺς ἦν π</span>.
			(v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψον</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
				<i>priests who had their meals at the public expense</i>,
				Clitodem.<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polem.Hist.
				78
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who dines with a superior officer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				551
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
